{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:87071",
  "title": "Important: php8.4 security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-22 00:08:23"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-22 00:12:16"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "PHP is an HTML-embedded scripting language. PHP attempts to make it easy for developers to write dynamically generated web pages. PHP also offers built-in database integration for several commercial and non-commercial database management systems, so writing a database-enabled webpage with PHP is fairly simple. The most common use of PHP coding is probably as a replacement for CGI scripts.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* php: php: Denial of Service via unbounded recursion in SOAP parser (CVE-2026-91765)\n\n* php: OOM bailout during request parsing leads to memory corruption and RCE (CVE-2026-109618)\n\n* php: fatal error handling retains stale request state leading to use-after-free (CVE-2026-109619)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
